 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding pages of the U.S. Embassy in Tokyo's monthly report on conditions in Japan for July 1940, a State Department Far Eastern Affairs Division memorandum reviewing August economic data, and the entirety of Despatch No. 5054 transmitting the August 1940 monthly report. The documents detail the fall of the Yonai Cabinet and the establishment of Prince Fumimaro Konoye's second Cabinet, highlighting the promulgation of the 'new national structure,' a sweeping reorganization of diplomatic personnel, and growing alignment with the Axis powers. Diplomatic and military friction with the United States and Great Britain is prominently featured, including disputes over Shanghai Defense Sectors, arrests of foreign nationals and journalists, military demands on French Indo-China, negotiations with the Netherlands East Indies, and expanding wartime economic and religious controls.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "Concluding portion of the Tokyo Embassy's monthly report for July 1940 covering the Cabinet change, economic conditions, pressure on American business, and monthly lists of telegrams and despatches sent to the Department.",
   "continues_previous": true,
   "date": "1940-07",
