   ],
   "start_page": 343,
   "summary": "This concluding segment of the July 1940 report reviews the resignation of the Yonai Cabinet on July 16 and the Emperor's command to Prince Fumimaro Konoye to form a new Cabinet, noting expectations of closer relations with the Axis and military authorities. It surveys domestic business and financial stagnation under newly enacted anti-luxury restrictions, which banned manufacture of non-essentials as of July 7 and sales from October 7. It also details mounting Japanese pressure on American firms, highlighting the Ministry of Commerce's attempt to force the American machine tool agency Andrews and George to sell out to German-controlled Sanyo Shokai. The report concludes with complete chronological lists of telegrams and despatches forwarded to the State Department during July 1940.",
   "title": "Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of July 1940",
   "to": "Department of State"
  },
  {
   "about": "State Department Division of Far Eastern Affairs memorandum summarizing the financial and economic sections of Tokyo's August 1940 monthly report.",
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1940-11-06",
   "doc_type": "memorandum",
   "end_page": 361,
   "from": "Division of Far Eastern Affairs",
   "keywords": [
    "Division of Far Eastern Affairs",
    "economic conditions",
    "Bank of Japan",
    "bond absorption",
    "price control",
    "yen bloc"
   ],
   "start_page": 360,
   "summary": "The memorandum observes that most political and diplomatic matters in Tokyo's monthly report for August 1940 had already reached the Division through earlier telegrams and despatches, focusing specifically on previously unreceived economic data. It notes growing apprehension in Japanese business circles regarding expanded state control and reports a weak stock market. It records that national bond absorption fell to 71 percent compared to 104.5 percent in July, Bank of Japan average daily note issues reached a new high, wholesale and retail prices advanced sharply, and Prime Minister Konoye announced stricter trade controls for the yen-bloc area.",
   "title": "Memorandum on Tokyo's Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of August 1940",
   "to": "Division of Far Eastern Affairs"
  },
  {
   "about": "Embassy despatch transmitting Report No. 167 on political, diplomatic, military, and economic conditions in Japan during August 1940, along with a list of despatches sent during the month.",
