   "start_page": 362,
   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits the Embassy's detailed monthly report on conditions in Japan for August 1940. Key external relations topics include diplomatic representations over the Shanghai Marine-Gendarme incident of July 7, American-Japanese disputes over reallocating the Shanghai Defense Sectors following British troop withdrawals, the detention and interrogation of AP correspondent Relman Morin, secret military demands presented to French Indo-China, anti-British sentiment and arrests, and the dispatch of Ichizo Kobayashi's mission to the Netherlands East Indies. Internally, the report analyzes the Konoye Cabinet's August 1 high policy proclamation, the 'new national structure' movement to assist the Throne, an unprecedented shakeup of Foreign Office and diplomatic personnel orchestrated by Foreign Minister Matsuoka and Vice Minister Ohashi, the establishment of the Cabinet Intelligence Bureau, and pressure on Christian churches to eliminate foreign leadership and funding. Appended to the report is a full chronological list of despatches sent to the Department during August 1940.",
   "title": "Despatch No. 5054: Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of August 1940",
   "to": "The Secretary of State, Washington"
  }
